{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation pushed to Gerrit as a 2-change stack:\n- change 1220 'd067: extract DC transition cluster' (pure move, no behaviour change)\n- change 1221 'd067: route DC outbound status to a transition' (the fix + tests)\n\nRED -> GREEN evidence\nBefore the fix, with --runxfail:\n  FAILED test_an_outbound_status_should_dispatch_the_transition_that_reaches_it\n  AssertionError: the outbound status 'In Progress' must resolve to transition\n  'Start Progress' (id 11) and be dispatched; got transitioned=[] and\n  edited_fields=[{'status': 'In Progress'}]\nAfter the fix, xfail(strict=True) marker REMOVED: 6 passed in\ntests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_dc_outbound_status_routing_5200.py.\nWhole reconciler unit suite: 1826 passed.\n\nMUTATED: reverted the status routing in JiraDataCenterTransport.update_issue\n(removed the status kwargs.pop and the route_status_to_transition call, restoring\nthe field-edit-only behaviour); FAILED:\ntests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_dc_outbound_status_routing_5200.py::test_an_outbound_status_should_dispatch_the_transition_that_reaches_it\nwith exactly:\n  AssertionError: the outbound status 'In Progress' must resolve to transition\n  'Start Progress' (id 11) and be dispatched; got transitioned=[] and\n  edited_fields=[{'status': 'In Progress'}]\nThat names the missing transition dispatch, not an AttributeError/ImportError, so\nthe mutation is VALID. All 4 tests in the file went RED under it; the code was\nrestored by hand (git diff --stat empty against the commit) and returned GREEN.\n\nIllegal transitions: NON-FATAL and OBSERVABLE\ntransitions.route_status_to_transition converts both shapes Jira serves for\n'illegal from the current state' -- the transition being absent from the\ntransitions list, and a listed transition rejected with 400 -- into\nIllegalTransitionError, which is deliberately NOT an HTTPError subclass.\napplier._apply_one (applier.py:757) re-raises urllib.error.HTTPError ABOVE its\nper-mutation backstop as a fail-fast contract, and BackendHTTPError subclasses it,\nso letting Jira's raw rejection escape would have aborted the whole pass over one\nissue in an unexpected state. Because IllegalTransitionError is an ordinary\nexception it reaches apply_handlers.record_backstop_failure instead, which writes a\nbridge_alerts record and lets the batch continue. Asserted by\ntest_an_illegal_transition_is_non_fatal_and_lands_in_bridge_alerts, which drives the\nREAL sequencer applier._apply_one over two mutations and checks (a) the follower\nstill dispatches and (b) a bridge_alerts JSONL entry exists naming the issue and the\nstatus. The observed record:\n  {\"kind\": \"mutation-error\", \"key\": \"DIG-1\", \"action\": \"update\", \"reason\":\n  \"outbound status 'In Progress' could not be applied to DIG-1: no transition\n  reaches it from the issue's current workflow state (...)\"}\nA contrast test pins that a 502 still propagates fail-fast, so the softening cannot\nbroaden into hiding an outage. Oracle validated: forcing _is_illegal_transition to\nreturn True turned that contrast test RED.\n\nMODULE SIZE\ntransport.py before: 746 / 800 (54 lines of headroom). After: 733.\nSeam extracted: the workflow-transition cluster that update_issue ->\nroute_status_to_transition -> resolve_transition -> client.transitions/\ntransition_issue already formed, moved to a new\nadapters/jira_datacenter/transitions.py (166 LOC, above the 100-LOC floor).\ntransport.py keeps transition_issue_by_name as a thin delegator and re-exports the\npublic names, mirroring how story f2f3/S1 extracted retry.py. No file in src/rebar\nexceeds 800.\n\nVendor attributes verified at RUNTIME against pycontribs/jira 3.10.5:\nJIRA.transitions=True, JIRA.transition_issue=True, Issue.update=True;\nBackendHTTPError('',400,'Illegal transition',...).code == 400 and\nstr() == 'HTTP Error 400: Illegal transition', so the 400-detection predicate\nmatches on the translated error."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785699812599295001,"uuid":"4e562f45-09be-45f4-8660-19d6958f9f61"}